:: ===========================================================================
::  Pulse run-tracking check-in  —  CONFIG TEMPLATE
:: ===========================================================================
::  Enables the "what VPUs has Pulse run on" list. On startup Pulse sends a
::  small identity-only beacon (hostname, serial, venue, model, version) to the
::  URL below; a Google Apps Script appends/updates one row per unit in a Sheet.
::
::  TO ENABLE:
::    1. Copy this file to "pulse-checkin.cfg" (same folder as run_pulse_beta.bat).
::    2. Fill in the two values below with your deployed Apps Script /exec URL
::       and the matching shared secret.
::    3. Hand testers run_pulse_beta.bat AND pulse-checkin.cfg together. On first
::       launch the launcher copies the .cfg into C:\Pulse, so Start-Menu launches
::       keep checking in. App auto-updates never overwrite it.
::
::  NOTES:
::    - pulse-checkin.cfg is gitignored — the filled copy must NEVER be committed.
::    - If this file is absent, check-in is simply disabled (Pulse runs normally).
::    - Demo/dev builds never check in, even if these are set.
:: ===========================================================================

set "PULSE_CHECKIN_URL=https://script.google.com/macros/s/PASTE_YOUR_DEPLOYMENT/exec"
set "PULSE_CHECKIN_SECRET=PASTE_YOUR_SHARED_SECRET"
